<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian sugar crush - week to July 26.</title>
<headline>Australian sugar crush - week to July 26.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's sugar cane crush totalled 1,622,543 tonnes in the week ended July 26, bringing the crush so far this season to 8.85 million tonnes, grower organisation CANEGROWERS said.</p>
<p>This is slightly lower than 9.14 million tonnes crushed at the same time last year. CANEGROWERS reported for crushing week eight of the 1997 season that average commercial cane sugar (ccs) content was 13.49 percent. The figures do not include cane crushed in the Ord River region of Western Australia.</p>
<p>Australian sugar cane crush by region for the week ended July 26 as reported by CANEGROWERS, in tonnes.  </p>
<p>CCS = Commercial Cane Sugar (sugar content percent)-</p>
<p>		    Crushed   Crushed     CCS	CCS</p>
<p>		    This wk   to Date   this wk  to date</p>
<p>North Qld	 408,829  2,315,742   12.81    12.09</p>
<p>Burdekin	  370,665  2,188,812   14.85    13.66</p>
<p>Central Qld     501,493  2,896,130   13.71    11.93</p>
<p>South Qld	 252,656    902,882   13.26    13.01</p>
<p>Queensland    1,533,643  8,303,566   13.67    12.41</p>
<p>N.South Wales    88,900    549,324   10.41    10.68</p>
<p>Australia     1,622,543  8,852,890   13.49    12.36</p>
<p>				   YEAR AGO</p>
<p>Queensland    1,669,105  8,853,574   12.97    12.41</p>
<p>Australia     1,767,381  9,139,750   12.85    12.36</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Summary - Total cane crushed 39.604 million tonnes (Qld 37.217 million, NSW 2.387 million), sugar produced 5.442 million tonnes 94 nt, (Qld 5.156 million, NSW 285,616), sugar content (CCS) 13.50 percent (Qld 13.62 percent, NSW 11.63 percent).</p>
